# %%title%%

A Trunk **%%type%%** application.

## Getting started

```bash
composer install
%%start%%
```

Application settings (`APP_ENV`, `APP_DEBUG`, `APP_PORT`, secrets...) live in `.env` (created for you, git-ignored;
`.env.example` is the committed template). Real environment variables override `.env`.

## Everyday commands

```bash
trunk list              # everything available
trunk doctor            # check the project is healthy
trunk make:service Name # generate code (controller, service, middleware, command, module, test)
trunk test              # run the tests
trunk build             # compile for production (then run with APP_ENV=production)
```

## What this application is made of

`trunk.php` lists the modules (capabilities) this application uses:

%%modules_md%%

Add or remove a module there and run `trunk doctor`. Nothing you do not list is loaded or compiled.

## Layout

```text
app/         your code (namespace App\)
config/      configuration (arrays, or closures receiving the Runtime)
%%layout%%storage/     caches and logs (not committed)
tests/       PHPUnit tests
trunk.php    the module list
```
